      "writtenOn": "2018-04-04T15:08:00Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a reason we do this here? It seems to me that it would be simpler to do this in isCaptivePortal(), or right after isCaptivePortal returns. That way, the flow is:\n\n- isCaptivePortal() does its HTTP and HTTPS probes. All DNS is cleartext.\n- If the probe fails, continue to do exponential backoff in EvaluatingState.\n- If the probe says portal, go into the captive portal state and sit there until the user logs in.\n- If the probe succeeds and we\u0027re in strict mode, immediately do the DNS lookup for the provider name. If that DNS lookup fails, then the network is unvalidated, and we continue to do exponential backoff in EvaluatingState.\n- If we\u0027re not in strict mode, or if the lookup succeeds, send a message to CS telling it to program the resolvers.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 795,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 795,
        "endChar": 62
      },
      "revId": "b5c6e5074f8e092bf0baf0edfb54f5eeecc61075",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
